<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konrad von Heresbach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1496">1496</a>–<a href="/years/1576">1576</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Konrad Heresbach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konrad von Heresbach was a German humanist, jurist and agricultural writer, a friend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erasmus">Erasmus</a> and tutor to the future Duke William of Jülich-Cleves-Berg. As counsellor to Duke John III he shaped a moderate, Erasmian church policy that sought reform without breaking with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> work on husbandry, Rei rusticae libri quattuor (1570), was translated into English and widely read.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konrad-von-heresbach.jpg" alt="Konrad von Heresbach" width="320" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konrad_heresbach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
